## Solution

**Interpretation.** By standard convention, $9^{9^9} = 9^{(9^9)}$. First compute the exponent:
$$9^9 = 387420489.$$

So we need the number of decimal digits of $9^{387420489}$.

**Digit-counting formula.** For any positive integer $N$, the number of decimal digits is
$$D(N) = \lfloor \log_{10} N \rfloor + 1.$$

Applying this:
$$D\!\left(9^{387420489}\right) = \lfloor \log_{10}\!\left(9^{387420489}\right) \rfloor + 1 = \lfloor 387420489 \cdot \log_{10} 9 \rfloor + 1.$$

**Computing the product.** Using $\log_{10} 9 = 0.95424250943932487459\ldots$, I evaluate $387420489 \times 0.9542425094393249$ by decomposing:

$$387420489 \times 0.9542425094393249 = 387420489 \times (1 - 0.0457574905606751).$$

Computing $387420489 \times 0.0457574905606751$ piece by piece:

| Term | Value |
|------|-------|
| $387420489 \times 0.04$ | $15496819.560$ |
| $387420489 \times 0.005$ | $1937102.445$ |
| $387420489 \times 0.0007$ | $271194.342$ |
| $387420489 \times 0.00005$ | $19371.024$ |
| $387420489 \times 0.000007$ | $2711.943$ |
| $387420489 \times 0.0000004$ | $154.968$ |
| $387420489 \times 0.00000009$ | $34.868$ |
| remaining ($\approx 0.00000000056$) | $\approx 0.217$ |

Summing these:
$$15496819.560 + 1937102.445 + 271194.342 + 19371.024 + 2711.943 + 154.968 + 34.868 + 0.217 \approx 17727389.367.$$

Therefore:
$$387420489 \times 0.9542425094393249 \approx 387420489 - 17727389.367 = 369693099.633.$$

**Robustness of the floor.** The fractional part is approximately $0.633$, which lies comfortably far from both $0$ and $1$. Even an error of $\pm 10^{-10}$ in $\log_{10} 9$ would shift the product by at most $387420489 \times 10^{-10} \approx 0.039$, nowhere near enough to change the floor. Thus:
$$\lfloor 387420489 \cdot \log_{10} 9 \rfloor = 369693099.$$

**Final answer.**
$$D\!\left(9^{9^9}\right) = 369693099 + 1 = \boxed{369693100}.$$

